# 1️⃣ Longest Increasing Subsequence (LIS)

## Problem

Find longest subsequence such that:

```text
arr[i]
<
arr[j]
```

for every next element.

---

### Example

```text
10 9 2 5 3 7 101 18
```

LIS:

```text
2 3 7 101
```

Length:

```text
4
```

---

# 2️⃣ DP State

```cpp
dp[i]
```

Meaning:

```text
Length of LIS
ending at i
```

---

# 3️⃣ Recurrence

For every previous element:

```cpp
if(arr[prev] < arr[i])
{
    dp[i]
    =
    max(
        dp[i],
        1 + dp[prev]
    );
}
```

---

### Code

```cpp
vector<int> dp(n,1);

for(int i=0;i<n;i++)
{
    for(int prev=0;
        prev<i;
        prev++)
    {
        if(arr[prev] < arr[i])
        {
            dp[i]
            =
            max(
                dp[i],
                1 + dp[prev]
            );
        }
    }
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N²)

Space: O(N)
```

---

# 4️⃣ LIS Using Binary Search

Optimized Solution.

Maintain:

```text
temp[]
```

---

### Idea

Store smallest possible tail.

---

### Code

```cpp
vector<int> temp;

temp.push_back(arr[0]);

for(int i=1;i<n;i++)
{
    if(arr[i] > temp.back())
    {
        temp.push_back(arr[i]);
    }
    else
    {
        int index =
        lower_bound(
            temp.begin(),
            temp.end(),
            arr[i]
        )
        -
        temp.begin();

        temp[index] = arr[i];
    }
}
```

---

### Complexity

```text
Time: O(N log N)

Space: O(N)
```

